================================================================================
Antigen — live DataHub run  (console transcript, verbatim)
================================================================================
This is the unedited console output of the DEMO.md "Live (against a real DataHub
GMS)" path, run end to end against a real GMS. The structured record of every SDK
call made during this same run is docs/live-tool-transcript.json.

  GMS                      http://localhost:8080  (v1.7.0, quickstart)
  GMS commit               7f81ccbfe27b9acc947f5f600fcf9ddb72138a80
  managed-ingestion CLI    1.6.0.6
  acryl-datahub            1.6.0.6
  datahub-agent-context    1.6.0.17
  auth                     metadata-service auth DISABLED (quickstart) -> DATAHUB_GMS_TOKEN empty
  captured                 2026-08-09T14:01:01Z

CYCLE A runs the hero arc (`python -m antigen demo --apply`).
CYCLE B resets and runs the reproducible proof (`python verify.py --live`), which
performs its own scan+cure and therefore needs a freshly poisoned graph.
CYCLE C resets, seeds the catalog past the live GMS's 50-row `search` page
(`python seed_catalog.py --scale 60`) and runs the read-only sweep, so the paging
loop in SdkGateway._paged_urns executes more than one page against a real server.

Home directory and username are replaced with placeholders. Nothing else is edited.
Two rough edges are left in on purpose: the reset before CYCLE C did not converge
(three KB documents were still in the search index after 120 s of hard-delete
polling, and it says so) — those three are why CYCLE C sweeps 78 entities and not
75. And CYCLE A sweeps 15 entities where the 2026-08-08 run swept 17: the two KB
documents seed_corpus.py plants are DOCUMENT entities that `search` returns once
OpenSearch has indexed them, and here it had not yet. Both KB payloads were found
regardless, through search_documents/grep_documents — 15/15 loci either way.

The previous capture (2026-08-08, before the --apply write gate and the 50-row
paging fix) is kept alongside this one as docs/live-run-2026-08-08.log and
docs/live-tool-transcript-2026-08-08.json.
